---
import DocPage from '../components/ui/DocPage.astro';
import OperatorBlock from '../components/ui/OperatorBlock.astro';
import { SITE, href } from '../data/site';
import { OPERATOR, CONTACTS } from '../data/operator';

const updated = 'October 12, 2026';
const ph = (v: string) => /\{\{/.test(v);
const toc: [string, string][] = [
  ['ownership', 'Your work is yours'],
  ['agreement', '1. Agreement'],
  ['eligibility', '2. Who can use Reelay'],
  ['beta', '3. Beta, free'],
  ['licence', '4. Licence'],
  ['acceptable-use', '5. Acceptable use'],
  ['your-posts', '6. What you post'],
  ['platforms', '7. Platforms you connect'],
  ['youtube', '8. YouTube features'],
  ['ai', '9. AI suggestions and agents'],
  ['data', '10. Your data and backups'],
  ['warranty', '11. No warranty'],
  ['liability', '12. Limitation of liability'],
  ['termination', '13. Termination'],
  ['law', '14. Governing law'],
  ['changes', '15. Changes'],
  ['contact', '16. Contact'],
];
---

<DocPage
  title="Terms of Service"
  pageTitle={`Terms of Service: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Reelay Studio Terms of Service: the beta, the licence, acceptable use, your responsibility for what you post, platform terms including YouTube's, and the legal fine print."
  updated={updated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">The agreement for using the Reelay Studio Mac app and this website. <strong>Plain where we could make it plain.</strong></Fragment>

  <section id="ownership" class="doc-summary">
    <h2>Your work is yours</h2>
    <p>Your videos, captions, transcripts, notes and everything else you make or keep in Reelay belong to you. Reelay claims no rights in them, and they stay on your Mac.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="agreement">
    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>These Terms are between you and <span class:list={[{ 'placeholder-token': ph(OPERATOR.legalEntity) }]}>{OPERATOR.legalEntity}</span> (“Reelay”, “we”, “us”). By downloading, installing or using the Reelay Studio app (the “Software”) or this website, you agree to them and to our <a href={href('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>. If you don’t agree, don’t install or use the Software.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="eligibility">
    <h2>2. Who can use Reelay</h2>
    <p>You must be at least 13 years old, and old enough to consent to the processing of your personal data where you live. To connect a business, creator or Page account on a platform that requires its users to be 18, you must be 18. If you use Reelay for an organisation or a creator you manage, you confirm you are authorised to bind them to these Terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="beta">
    <h2>3. Beta, free</h2>
    <p>Reelay {SITE.version} is a beta. It is free to use, and there is no account to create with us. Features may change or stop working, including when a platform changes its rules or withdraws an approval. Pricing after the beta has not been set; if we introduce paid plans, they won’t apply to you unless you accept them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="licence">
    <h2>4. Licence</h2>
    <p>We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use the Software on Macs you own or control, for your own content work or work for creators you manage. You may not sell, rent or redistribute the Software, remove its notices, or reverse engineer it except where the law allows you to.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Reelay is for media you own or are authorised to manage. You agree:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>to import, download and republish only videos, sounds and other material you own or are authorised to manage;</li>
      <li>to follow the terms, community guidelines and developer policies of every platform you use through Reelay;</li>
      <li>to record accurate permission and provenance details when you set them on a ticket;</li>
      <li>not to use Reelay to infringe anyone’s copyright, trademark, privacy or other rights, or to break any law;</li>
      <li>not to use Reelay to send spam, to get around a platform’s limits or safety systems, or to bypass Reelay’s approval step, Ready gate or Agent API key.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To report content you believe infringes your rights, see <a href={href('/copyright')}>Copyright</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-posts">
    <h2>6. What you post</h2>
    <p>You are responsible for everything you publish or schedule with Reelay, wherever it is posted, including captions, hashtags, sounds and the videos themselves. Reelay prepares and sends what you approve; it doesn’t review your content.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="platforms">
    <h2>7. Platforms you connect</h2>
    <p>When you connect an account, your use of that platform through Reelay is also governed by its own terms: TikTok’s Terms of Service; Meta’s Terms and the terms of Instagram, Threads and Facebook; Snap’s Terms of Service; and Bluesky’s Terms of Service. Reelay talks to these platforms on your behalf from your Mac. We aren’t responsible for a platform’s decisions about your account, its rate limits, its review of a post, or changes to its API. Reelay isn’t affiliated with or endorsed by any of them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="youtube">
    <h2>8. YouTube features</h2>
    <p>Reelay uses YouTube API Services. <strong>By using Reelay’s YouTube features, you agree to be bound by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.</strong> Google’s use of your data is described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>, and you can remove Reelay’s access at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="ai">
    <h2>9. AI suggestions and agents</h2>
    <p>Writing help and any AI agent you connect produce suggestions. They can be wrong, and you decide whether to use them. You are responsible for reviewing AI-written text before it is published, for the automation rules you create, and for the requests you approve. If you connect an agent that uses a third-party AI service, that service’s terms apply to it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="data">
    <h2>10. Your data and backups</h2>
    <p>Reelay keeps your data on your Mac and not on our servers, so we can’t restore it for you. Back up your video files and Reelay’s database yourself. How to find, move or delete that data is in the <a href={href('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href={href('/data-deletion')}>Data Deletion Instructions</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="warranty">
    <h2>11. No warranty</h2>
    <p>THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SOFTWARE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED OR ERROR-FREE, OR THAT ANY PLATFORM WILL CONTINUE TO WORK WITH IT. Some places don’t allow these exclusions, so some may not apply to you.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, REELAY AND ITS CONTRIBUTORS WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, USE OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE. BECAUSE THE BETA IS FREE, OUR TOTAL LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY CLAIM IS LIMITED TO <span class:list={[{ "placeholder-token": ph(OPERATOR.liabilityCap) }]}>{OPERATOR.liabilityCap}</span>. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that can’t be limited by law.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="termination">
    <h2>13. Termination</h2>
    <p>You can stop using Reelay at any time by deleting it and its data (see <a href={href('/data-deletion')}>Data Deletion</a>). We may end your licence if you break these Terms. Sections 5, 6 and 10 to 14 survive termination.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
    <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of <span class:list={[{ 'placeholder-token': ph(OPERATOR.governingLaw) }]}>{OPERATOR.governingLaw}</span>, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules. This doesn’t take away any protection you have under the mandatory consumer laws of the country where you live.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>15. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these Terms. We will change the date at the top and note it in the <a href={href('/changelog')}>Changelog</a>. If you keep using the Software after an update, the updated Terms apply.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
    <OperatorBlock />
    <p>Questions about these Terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.reviewers}`}>{CONTACTS.reviewers}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</DocPage>
